WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.935
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.771
And now, if you don't mind,
we're gonna get to the news.

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:08.273
President Biden is reportedly
considering raising tariffs

00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:09.609
on some Chinese goods.

00:00:09.609 --> 00:00:12.111
Biden came up with the idea
the moment he realized

00:00:12.111 --> 00:00:14.147
his fingers were stuck.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:16.316
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:18.384
Well, it's our last show
of the year,

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.286
so let's take a minute
to look back

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.722
on all the best moments
of 2023.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:26.225
-Rudy Giuliani
to pay $148 million.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.861
-Rudy Giuliani, $148 million.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.063
-Rudy Giuliani, $148 million.

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:33.599
-$148 million.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.201
-$148 million.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:37.436
$148 million.

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:38.972
-What a year.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.473
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.408
Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis yesterday

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:45.045
criticized the biblical city
of Bethlehem

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.847
and said it was
a "pigsty and disgrace."

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:50.650
Even worse,
he did it while caroling.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.484
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.484 --> 00:00:54.019
A federal judge ruled yesterday

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:56.021
that the two Georgia
election workers who won

00:00:56.021 --> 00:00:59.792
a $148 million defamation
judgment against Rudy Giuliani

00:00:59.792 --> 00:01:03.462
may expedite their payout
because they have good cause

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.831
that Giuliani might try
to avoid paying them.

00:01:05.831 --> 00:01:07.834
How did they come
to that conclusion?

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:10.670
Did they look
at any picture of him?

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.204
He definitely looks like a guy

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:14.173
who carries a quarter
on a string

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:16.843
so he can use payphones
for free.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.844
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.844 --> 00:01:20.613
Authorities in Georgia
are looking for a woman

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.282
who allegedly posed
as a Waffle House employee,

00:01:23.282 --> 00:01:24.817
worked at the restaurant
for two hours,

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.786
and then stole cash
from the register.

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:29.054
A spokesman for Waffle House
is calling her

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:31.190
employee of the month.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.858
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.858 --> 00:01:34.193
According to a new study,

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:36.529
Tesla drivers have
the highest accident rate.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.464
In fact, one of them
accidentally crashed

00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:40.967
an entire social media site.

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.802
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.470
The FAA said that it expects

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.206
holiday air travel
will peak today.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.340
Okay, but what
do they mean "expect"?

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.242
We all bought our tickets
a long time ago.

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:51.644
You could just check.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.413
Is anybody showing up
to the airport

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.281
on December 21st on a whim?

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.615
"Yeah, you know,
I just came out here

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:59.419
to have dinner at Chili's,
and then, you know,

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:03.089
I thought, hell, maybe I'll fly
to Orlando, you know?

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.592
Everybody else
seems to be doing it."

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.026
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:10.930
A city in California held
a contest to name its snow plow,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:13.766
and the winning name
was "The Big Leplowski."

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.102
As opposed to Boston,
who went with

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.803
"I Plowed Ya Mutha."

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:20.840
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.513
CNN published a list this week

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:30.249
of the worst-behaved tourists
of 2023,

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:32.852
but I don't even need to read it
to know what was number one,

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:35.855
because I'm living it
every single day.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.091
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.761
People work here!

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:44.263
People of business
are doing business!

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.532
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.301
And finally, the billionaire
heir

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.470
to the luxury goods company
Hermès

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.805
has reportedly filed
to legally adopt

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:54.106
his middle-aged gardener

00:02:54.106 --> 00:02:56.776
and leave him half
of his $13 billion fortune.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.779
And I think we actually have
a photo of the gardener.

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:01.447
George!

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.115
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:05.785
That was a monologue, everybody.
We're off and running.

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.887
Off and running.

